      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "EIA was used to demonstrate that the development of acute ischemia of the heart muscle progressing to necrosis is accompanied by an increase of the concentration of cytochrome c and antibodies against cytochrome c in the blood serum. As regards its specificity and sensitivity, the alteration in the antibody concentration is comparable with that in the myoglobin concentration but it is marked 1 to 3 hours earlier. The high level of antibodies against cytochrome c remaining unchanged for 2 to 3 days in myocardial infarction patients attests to the possibility of a complicated, often relapsing course of the disease. The test for determining antibodies against cytochrome c may be recommended for the control over the patient's status and forecasting the course of myocardial infarction."},
